//     dependency of this repo) instead of go-runewidth, so the package adds no
//     new module.
//   - Sub-zone support: a zone marked inside another zone records its parent and
//     can report a parent-local rectangle via [ZoneInfo.LocalBounds], for widgets
//     that do internal sub-region layout/hit-testing (the CycleField option strip
//     and the FilterBar click-target row land on this in t2_3).
//
// # Parity contract
//
// Scan strips every marker, so the terminal and the parity goldens only ever see
// clean text. The markers are zero-width CSI sequences (ESC '[' <n> 'z') that
// lipgloss / x/ansi width methods ignore, and that parity/normalize.sh neither
